  "reviewer": {
    "review_summary": "The planner, backend, and frontend specifications are well aligned and collectively describe a coherent LabFlow system for student lab submissions and teacher reviews. Core entities, workflow, API contracts, data model, UI components, and metrics are consistently defined, enabling implementation of the required functionality.",
    "strengths": [
      "Clear definition of roles, statuses, and workflow steps that match across planner and backend validation rules.",
      "Comprehensive REST API covering creation, submission, review, resubmission, and metrics retrieval.",
      "Consistent data fields between planner primary_fields and backend storage_fields, supporting audit history.",
      "Frontend UI outlines necessary dashboards, forms, tables, and detail views to manage labs, submissions, and analytics.",
      "Seed data and validation rules provide concrete examples for testing and ensure data integrity."
    ],
    "risks": [
      "Frontend focuses on admin/dashboard views and lacks explicit student and teacher interaction screens (e.g., submission form, review form).",
      "The API does not include endpoints for managing labs, users, or authentication, which are implied by the planner and UI.",
      "Decision values include \"needs_resubmission\" but backend status list uses \"needs_resubmission\"; ensure consistent naming across all layers.",
      "No explicit handling of file uploads (attachment URLs) in the API; front‑end may need a separate upload service.",
      "Audit/logging details are mentioned but no endpoint for retrieving raw audit logs beyond history_log field."
    ],
    "adjustments": [
      "Add frontend view specifications for Student Submission Form and Teacher Review Form, including required fields and actions.",
      "Introduce backend endpoints for Lab management (GET/POST/PUT /api/v1/labs) and User management (auth, role assignment).",
      "Standardize decision/status naming (e.g., use \"needs_resubmission\" uniformly) across planner, backend, and frontend.",
      "Specify an upload endpoint (e.g., POST /api/v1/submissions/{id}/attachments) or integrate with a storage service for handling attachment files.",
      "Provide an endpoint for detailed audit logs (e.g., GET /api/v1/submissions/{id}/audit) if more granular traceability is required."
    ]
  }
